So I don't know what your criteria are for "hit" - if it's just physical skills, anything anyone does to damage the enemy, etc.
But on a basic level, you'd do something like this in the state. I'm pretending Robbie is actor ID 1.
Code:
<Custom Respond Effect>
// Is the attacker NOT Robbie?
if (user.actorId() != 1)
{
// Make Robbie attack
    $gameActors.actor(1).forceAction(1, target.index());
    BattleManager.forceAction($gameActors.actor(1));
}
</Custom Respond Effect>
When you get into talking about the CTB and stuff, the risk can be that using force action might take up that battler's next actual action; so you might have to do something like incorporating this into an action sequence.
But this ought to do something.

