One extra thing actually-- I have a skill type in my game called "followup" reserved for any followup attack. is there a way I could check if the damage is NOT followup type just so that the player doesn't have followup attacks triggering each other endlessly?
I tried editing the code, but it didn't work for me.
JavaScript:
<Custom Respond Effect>

// Is the attacker NOT Robbie?

if (user.actorId() != 22){

if (skill.stypeId() !=5)

{

// Make Robbie attack

    $gameActors.actor(22).forceAction(50, target.index());

    BattleManager.forceAction($gameActors.actor(22));

}}

</Custom Respond Effect>
I wrote if (skill.stypeId != 5) but that just stopped the followup from triggering at all. I imagine I'm not supposed to use "skill" but I couldn't find out how to write this looking through the RPG maker library.

