its not the only resource youd need in this case. once you start dealing with stuff introduced by plugins, youd also have to be mindful of what the plugin says and does either by reading the documentation or looking into the plugin itself if the documentation is lacking.
respond effects are ran from the Game_Action triggering it, so you would want to do something like
Code:
if (user.actorId() != 22 && this.item().stypeId!=5){
    // Make Robbie attack
    $gameActors.actor(22).forceAction(50, target.index());
    BattleManager.forceAction($gameActors.actor(22));
}

